The ideal candidate will have strong coordination skills, good judgment, a service-oriented mindset, and the ability to handle a wide range of family and household matters with professionalism, care, and confidentiality.

Key Responsibilities

1. Family and Household Coordination

Oversee and coordinate daily household operations to ensure the family’s routines run smoothly;

Manage calendars, appointments, reminders, and scheduling for family-related matters;

Coordinate transportation, medical appointments, errands, shopping, maintenance, and service bookings;

Assist with household purchasing, supplies management, and daily expense tracking where required;

Handle ad hoc family matters and provide timely follow-up on outstanding items.

2. Children’s Support and Scheduling

Arrange and manage school pick-up/drop-off, extracurricular activities, tutoring schedules, and other child-related logistics;

Support the planning and coordination of the children’s daily routines and activities;

Accompany or assist with appointments, registrations, school events, and enrichment programs as needed;

Monitor children’s day-to-day arrangements and provide timely updates to parents;

Offer practical support in childcare-related matters within the scope authorized by the family.

3. School Communication and Administrative Support

Serve as one of the key points of contact between the household and the children’s schools;

Follow up on school notices, forms, event registrations, and other school administrative matters;

Coordinate parent-teacher meetings, school events, and academic or activity-related schedules;

Maintain clear and professional communication with teachers, school administrators, and external providers when needed.

