Established in 1966, the Hong Kong Trade Development Council (HKTDC) is a statutory body that promotes, assists and develops Hong Kong’s trade, with the support of our 51 offices worldwide.

We help businesses large and small connect with growth and collaboration opportunities globally, while highlighting Hong Kong’s unique strengths and advantages and reinforcing its dual role as SUPER-CONNECTOR and super value-adder, linking China and the world.

We do so via our international trade fairs, industry conferences and industry missions, offering innovative offline-online event experiences. From embarking on missions to staging Hong Kong pavilions at leading mainland and overseas fairs as well as roadshows, our outreach also fosters opportunities and strengthens ties with the Chinese Mainland and our many international trading partners.

In a world marked by constant change, our programmes provide comprehensive tailor-made support to help businesses, in particular SMEs and start-ups, be future-ready and thrive. Complementing this, our research reports and digital news channels offer the latest market information to enable businesses to make informed business decisions and accelerate their expansion plans.

As we celebrate our 60th anniversary in 2026 and begin a new three-year business cycle, our mission remains as strong as ever to help Hong Kong thrive in trade and businesses succeed in the ever-changing landscape.”

We are seeking a dynamic, high-caliber, and experienced professional to join our Exhibitions and Digital Business Department.

The appointee will lead event operations and content delivery across trade fairs and related projects, ensuring seamless execution from planning to post-event review. The role combines end‑to‑end event operations management with content development and editorial oversight to deliver high-quality, timely and compliant outputs across physical and digital platforms.

 

Key Responsibilities

Event Operations Management

Lead end‑to‑end operational planning and execution of fairs and related projects, including production, logistics coordination, timelines and delivery control;

Oversee production for fairs and advertising assets (e.g. show collateral, on-site materials, digital assets), including budgeting, cost estimation, tendering and vendor management;

Manage cross-functional coordination across internal teams, agencies and vendors to ensure alignment, quality delivery and adherence to timelines;

Monitor project risks and operational issues proactively and drive timely resolution to minimize disruption to event delivery;

Support post-event evaluation, reporting and continuous improvement of operational workflows and delivery standards.

Content & Editorial Management

Plan, develop and edit fair-related, marketing and sponsored content for print and digital platforms, ensuring consistency with editorial standards, house style and platform policies;

Provide editorial oversight across event content outputs, including exhibitor listings, show guides, promotional materials and digital content;

Conduct research, interviews and fact-checking to ensure accuracy, relevance and quality of content;

Produce event coverage and post-event reports, capturing key insights and outcomes.

Process & Governance

Drive workflow optimization and operational improvements to enhance efficiency and scalability of event delivery and content production;

Maintain proper documentation, approvals and records to support governance, quality assurance and continuity;

Support preparation of management reports, summaries and analysis for planning and decision-making;

Undertake ad hoc projects and cross-team initiatives as assigned.

Requirements

Bachelor’s degree in Event Management, Communications, Digital Media, Marketing or a related discipline;

Minimum 5 years’ relevant experience in event / fair operations and content production, preferably in a trade fair or exhibition environment;

Strong project and operations management capability, with proven experience managing multiple concurrent projects under tight timelines;

Excellent command of written English and Chinese, with strong editorial judgement and attention to detail;

Strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with ability to work across functions and external partners;

Hands-on experience with Content Management System platforms, SEO practices and AI-enabled tools to enhance content operations and workflow efficiency;

Understanding of Hong Kong and Mainland China trade, business and economic landscape is an advantage.

